  "subject": "🦋 Axios Finish Line: The Dolly effect",
  "date": "Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:29:23 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🌊 Plus: Bye, summer! | Wednesday, September 23, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PRESENTED BY SUNTORY \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Sep 23, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 289 words … 1 min. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: Dolly Parton&#x27;s legacy sparks a giving wave \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n A portrait of Dolly Parton fills a 5-acre corn maze at Twins BBQ Co. in Brookfield, Conn., on Sept. 13. Photo: Ted Shaffrey/AP Dolly Parton spent her life giving back to children and their communities. Since her death, her fans have been carrying on that legacy.\n\n It's the Dolly effect: In cities across America, people are donating their time and money, expanding Dolly's Imagination Library — her book-gifting program for kids — and starting projects of their own. 📚 The big picture: Dolly started the Imagination Library in 1995 to honor her father, who couldn't read or write. The program sends over 3 million free books to children across five countries each month — and organizations and individuals are building on that legacy to reach even more.\n\n In Florida , Virginia , Ohio and elsewhere, Imagination Library affiliates have seen a surge in both donations and registrations since the star's passing on Aug. 25. In Houston, public libraries are working with the Imagination Library of Greater Houston to help more families sign up their children. In West Virginia, literacy nonprofit Read Aloud West Virginia is matching this month's donations to local Imagination Library affiliates when donors write \"in memory of Dolly\" with their contributions. In London, Dolly's Imagination Library is doubling the number of boroughs it covers. 🎸 What's next: This Friday — 9/25, a nod to Dolly's \"9 to 5\" movie — will be the first annual Give Like Dolly Day, created by The Dollywood Foundation to encourage people around the world to support children's literacy.\n\n One Nashville honky-tonk is giving 100% of Friday's sales to the Imagination Library and Nashville Public Libraries. \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM SUNTORY\r\n\n \r\n Healthy forests can help protect water supplies \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Suntory is looking upstream to help protect the groundwater its business and local communities depend on.\n\n\r\n Here’s how: Its 27 Natural Water Sanctuaries across Japan conserve forests and biodiversity while replenishing more than twice the groundwater used by its plants.\n\n\r\n See how. \n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🚤 Parting shot! \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Edward Fine It's officially fall, but we have one more stunning summer snap from reader Edward Fine — taken in Barnegat Light in Long Beach Island, N.J.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;